  "如果投手直接公开最终落点，打者只要照着画格子。因此，这套规则先公开起始标记，最后再揭球种：同一个标记，可以留在原位，也可能因球种移动。": "If the final location were public, the batter could simply cover it. Instead, the rules reveal the starting mark first and the pitch type last: the same mark may stay in place or move with the pitch.",
  "前几球也会影响判断。同样的标记上次用了变化球，这次会不会重复？投手同样可以利用打者已经形成的预期。": "Earlier pitches shape the decision too. A breaking ball followed this mark last time—will it happen again? The pitcher can also play against the batter’s expectations.",
