  "若这一方向只有一名相关守备球员，前一种情况形成安打，后一种情况让打者出局。若有多人参与，则必须所有相关球员都失败，才形成安打。": "With only one relevant fielder, the first case produces a hit and the second an out. With multiple fielders, all must fail for a hit to occur.",
  "球员卡 · 人物、位置与技能": "Player cards · People, positions and abilities",
  "球员卡组 · 不同球员形成不同阵容": "Player deck · Different players create different lineups",
  "阵容配置 · 安排球员与守备位置": "Lineup setup · Assign players to fielding positions",
  "阵容调整因此有了实际用途": "Lineup changes now have a practical purpose",
  "玩家不仅要判断这一球能否击中，也要留意它会打向哪里、那里由谁守备。防守方在每个攻守回合开始时，可以调整位置或换上一名替补；替补接替原来的棒次。调整后，该方向参与判定的球员和能力也会变化。": "Players must consider both whether they can connect and where the ball will go—and who fields there. At the start of each offensive or defensive half, the defender may adjust positions or bring in the substitute, who inherits the batting slot. The relevant fielders and abilities change accordingly.",
  "球员卡来自我的校队，但我希望他们在游戏里也有不同作用。守备力与技能让“选谁上场”产生规则上的后果，而不只是在图板上换一张照片。": "The cards depict my university team, but I wanted each teammate to play a distinct role. Fielding ratings and abilities give roster choices consequences in the rules, beyond changing a photograph on the board.",
  "守备分支与跑垒得分图解": "Fielding branches & baserunning diagrams",
  "图解 E · 普通击中后的守备分支；一格命中不走这一流程": "Diagram E · Fielding after normal contact; single-cell contact bypasses this process",
  "图解 F · 一垒打：打者上一垒，队友各推进一垒；回本垒得分": "Diagram F · Single: batter reaches first, teammates advance one base; reaching home scores a run",
  "为什么只有最后三局": "Why only the final three innings?",
  "每球都要画格子、出牌、揭牌和结算。早期九局版约一个半小时，操作重复让整场比赛太长。": "Every pitch requires marking grids, playing cards, revealing and resolving. The early nine-inning version took about 90 minutes; repeated actions made the full game too long.",
